<title>DENMARK: FORECAST-Lehman Bros see lower Danish 96 GDP, CPI.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Lehman Bros see lower Danish 96 GDP, CPI.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey U.S. investment bank Lehman Brothers on Tuesday cut its expectations for Denmark's 1996 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 1.7 percent from 2.5 percent in its December 1995 forecast.</p>
<p>At the same time it reduced its forecast for inflation to 2.1 percent from 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in August foresaw 1.8 percent GDP growth, 2.0 percent inflation, 9.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 10.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>		(pct)  GDP    inflation unemployment  c/a (bln crns)</p>
<p>Lehman Bros (8/96) 1.7    2.1	  8.9	     --</p>
<p>M.Grenfell (8/96)  1.5    2.1	  9.0	    12.0</p>
<p>Indosuez (8/96)    2.2    2.2	  8.9	    19.0</p>
<p>Chase (8/96)	 1.4    1.9	  --		8.0</p>
<p>Goldman Sachs(8/96)1.6    2.0	  9.3	    10.5</p>
<p>Nykredit (8/96)    1.4    2.1	  9.0	    10.0</p>
<p>Jyske Bank (8/96)  2.0    2.1	  9.0	     6.0</p>
<p>BG Bank (7/96)     2.0    2.0	  9.0	     6.0</p>
<p>Barclays (7/96)    1.5    2.0	  9.2	     6.0</p>
<p>Svenska HB (7/96)  1.5    2.2	  9.0	    10.0</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
